Z||000000||black86gt||03-14-99||05:44 PM||||Well, I am going to be getting a power pulley from the fiero store in a few days here and wanted to ask you guys something.  First, anyone have one and get any problems form it?  Will I get the 8hp it is said to give?  About how long will the install take?  I work slow...  Thanks guys.
Z||000001||Pretender||03-21-99||02:22 AM||||the power pulley from superchip?...when i called the "fiero store" and inquired about it the sales person said it would only give me a 2 horsepower increase so i didn't purchase it....did he tell you 8?...just wondering...my friends mustang 5.0 has them and it/they do work, so i would guess they should free up some power in our applicatons.............
Z||000002||black86gt||03-21-99||08:47 PM||||No I did not call them about it, but their catalog says 8hp increase (6% they say)
Z||000003||theogre||03-28-99||03:52 PM||||You will likely want to get the next size shorter fan belt..... most of the time a change in pully size makes the belts not fit. If you have the serpent belt this is especially critical as the serpent tensioner has a specific desined tension range that it will work correctly in, and a smaller pully WILL make the belt too big for the tensioner to keep it correctly tight.
Z||000004||mrfiero||03-28-99||06:20 PM||||I bought one of the Fiero Stores power pulleys about 4 years ago.  I noticed a little power increase.....not much, but coupled with other mods it helps (every little bit counts, right?).  It also included a new belt, so I don't think you'll need to buy one. 
